course: dictionary
lesson: 4571
title: Heir and the next in line
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An heir is the person who will get something next. «She is heir to the farm» means that when the owner dies, the farm will become hers. The words around heir give you clues: farm, property and "next" all point to getting something from someone.
explain: In history, heir often means the person who will rule next. «The heir to Austria-Hungary's throne, Archduke Franz Ferdinand, was shot in Sarajevo» tells you that he was next in line to be ruler. Throne is the clue: a throne belongs to a king or queen.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "the person who will get it next" in place of heir, and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: An heir is a person who will receive someone's money, house or other property when that person dies.
fact: The heir to the throne is the person who will become king or queen next.
fact: An heir can also be someone who carries on another person's work or ideas.
fact: Heir sounds the same as air, but it is spelled differently and has a different meaning.
fact: The plural of heir is heirs, meaning more than one heir.
exercise: «She is heir to the farm.» What does heir mean here? | A person who sells farm animals | A tractor driver who works all day | *A person who will get the farm when the owner dies
exercise: Who is the heir to the throne? | A person who sits on a throne in a museum | The person who cleans the palace | *The next person to become king or queen
exercise: Which word is the plural of heir? | heirish | *heirs | heirer | heirses
exercise: Hint: say it aloud. Which word sounds the same as heir but means the air we breathe? | hair | hear | hire | *air
test: «After Yaroslav his heirs quarrelled.» What does heirs mean here? | *The people who would take over his rule and lands after him | A group of quarrelsome soldiers from the north | Cooks who worked in the kitchen
test: Which sentence uses heir correctly? | I went to the heir to buy a loaf of bread | *The old king had no son, so he worried about who his heir would be | The dog wagged its heir
exam: Mia's grandad has a big farm and tells her, «You are my heir.» What does Mia now know? | She is not allowed to visit the farm | She has to work on the farm for one day only | She must pay grandad every year to use the farm | *She will get the farm when grandad dies
